BLOCKED by a Phase-1 regression (uncommitted feat/runner-memory-accounting):
resolving/registering a `custom:` runner inside a spawned sub-VM (sandbox or
nondet child) overflows the async-fiber stack ("execution on async fiber has
overflowed its stack"). Root-VM custom registration is fine (see
register_ladder). The pre-existing sandbox_custom_runner and nondet_custom_runner
cases fail identically on this tree, so it is not this case's contract.

This case asserts ADR-012 §4 no-flow-back (a sandbox-scoped RegisterRunner is
not resolvable in the parent). It is correct as written and should pass once the
sub-VM custom-runner stack overflow is fixed — remove this .skip then.
